==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|ey|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|ǣġ}} ("egg"; {{term/t|ang|ǣġru}} in the plural), from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*ajją}}, {{term/t|gem-pro|*ajjaz||egg}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ōuyo-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₂ōwyóm||egg}}. Cognate with {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|aai||egg|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|ei||egg|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|nds-de|-}} {{term|Ei||egg|lang=nds-de}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Ei||egg|lang=de}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|æg||egg|lang=da}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|ägg||egg|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|egg||egg|lang=is}}, {{etyl|gd|-}} {{term|ugh||egg|lang=gd}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{term/t|la|ōvum||egg}}. Was replaced by {{term|egg|lang=en}} in the 16th century.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|eyren}} (''obsolete since the sixteenth century'')

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} an [[egg]]

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{term|eyot|lang=en}}.

